LOK: a save leaves an open cell edit alone

PreDoSaveAs_Impl ended Calc's cell edit before every LOK save, copies
and recovery saves included (TerminateEditing commits the input). Keys
typed after a background save then started a new edit that replaced the
cell. Upstream Calc keeps the edit open on its own autosave for this
reason (ScDocShell::PrepareSaveGuard).

Now a save writes the cells as entered and the edit stays open. The
"TerminateEditing" save option enters it first, for a save that ends
the view. An entry Calc would discard stays open and the save fails
with a reason (TerminateEditing now says whether the edit ended), so a
close never drops it: one its validity rule refuses (any style but a
shown info message, which lets it in), or input into a pivot table. While a cell edit holds typed text,
LOK keeps the document modified, so a save no longer clears it. LOK
marked it modified on the first key only; text typed through
postExtTextInputEvent (how clients type characters) now marks it too.
A composition that opened an edit on a cell and ends empty (an IME
cancel) cancels the edit, as Escape does, so no later commit empties
the cell. The modified state stays, as after a key and Escape: other
changes may have landed meanwhile.

